REGIONAL REGULATION OF GORONTALO CITY

NUMBER 7 OF 2016

CONCERNING

PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN AGAINST VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE

BY THE GRACE OF GOD ALMIGHTY

MAYOR OF GORONTALO,

Considering:

a. that Pancasila and the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia guarantee the right of every citizen to be free from torture or treatment that degrades human dignity and to obtain a sense of security and freedom from all forms of violence;
b. that all forms of violence against women and children constitute violations of human rights so that their dignity and honor need to be protected and their right to life guaranteed in accordance with their nature and destiny without discrimination;
c. that women's empowerment and child protection are concurrent governmental affairs delegated to the regions to become the basis for implementing regional autonomy and become mandatory governmental affairs not related to basic services as referred to in Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government;
d. that in order to provide regulatory strengthening, direction, and foundation in the protection of women and children victims of violence, regulation is needed related to the Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence;
e. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, letter c, letter d, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence;

In View of:

1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 29 of 1959 concerning the Establishment of Level II Regions in Sulawesi (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1959 Number 74, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 1822);
3. Law Number 38 of 2000 concerning the Establishment of Gorontalo Province (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2000 Number 258, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4060);
4. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235) as amended several times most recently by Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 1 of 2016 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2016 Number 99, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5882);
5. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);
6. Law Number 13 of 2006 concerning the Protection of Witnesses and Victims (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2006 Number 64, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4635);
7. Law Number 21 of 2007 concerning the Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2007 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720);
8. Law Number 12 of 2011 concerning the Formulation of Legislation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2011 Number 82, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5234);
9. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as amended several times, most recently by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);
10. Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 concerning the Implementation and Cooperation for the Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 64);
11. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 01 of 2010 concerning Minimum Service Standards (SPM) for Integrated Services for Women and Children Victims of Violence;
12. Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 80 of 2015 concerning the Formulation of Regional Legal Products;

With Mutual Approval

REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF GORONTALO CITY

and

MAYOR OF GORONTALO

DECIDES:

To Establish:

REGIONAL REGULATION CONCERNING THE PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE.

text:
Pasal 2

Perlindungan Korban berasaskan:
a. penghormatan dan pemenuhan terhadap hak-hak korban;
b. keadilan dan kesetaraan gender;
c. non diskriminasi;
d. kepentingan terbaik bagi korban; dan
e. pemberdayaan.

translated_text:
Article 2

Protection of Victims is based on:
a. respect and fulfillment of the rights of victims;
b. justice and gender equality;
c. non-discrimination;
d. the best interests of victims; and
e. empowerment.

text:
BAB 11

BENTU K KEKER/LSA N

Pasal 5

Bentuk kekerasan antara lain:
a. kekerasan fisik;
b. kekerasan psikis;
c. kekerasan seksual;
d. penelantaran;
e. eksploitasi; dan/atau
f. kekerasan lainnya.

translated_text:
CHAPTER 11

FORMS OF VIOLENCE

Article 5

Forms of violence include:
a. physical violence;
b. psychological violence;
c. sexual violence;
d. neglect;
e. exploitation; and/or
f. other violence.

text:
Pasal 8

Kekerasan seksual sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 5 huruf c disebabkan karena:
a. perbuatan yang berupa pelecehan seksual;
b. pemaksaan hubungan seksual;
c. pemaksaan hubungan seksual dengan tidak wajar atau tidak disukai; dan/atau
d. pemaksaan hubungan seksual dengan orang lain untuk tujuan komersial dan atau tujuan tertentu.

translated_text:
Article 8

Sexual violence as referred to in Article 5 letter c is caused by:
a. acts in the form of sexual harassment;
b. forced sexual intercourse;
c. forced sexual intercourse in an unnatural or unwanted manner; and/or
d. forced sexual intercourse with others for commercial purposes and or certain purposes.

text:
Pasal 9

Penelantaran sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 5 huruf d disebabkan karena:
a. perbuatan yang mengakibatkan tidak terpenuhinya kebutuhan anak  secara wajar, baik fisik, mental, spiritual maupun sosial yang dilakukan oleh orang tua, wali, atau pihak lain manapun yang bertanggung jawab  atas pengasuhannya;
b. perbuatan mengabaikan dengan sengaja untuk memelihara, merawat,  atau mengurus anak sebagaimana mestinya yang dilakukan oleh orang tua, wali, atau pihak lain manapun yang bertanggung jawab atas  pengasuhannya;
c. perbuatan yang menelantarkan orang dalam lingkup rumah tangganya, padahal menurut hukum yang berlaku baginya atau karena persetujuan atau perjanjian ia wajib memberikan kehidupan, perawatan, atau  pemeliharaan kepada orang tersebut; dan/atau
d. perbuatan yang mengakibatkan ketergantungan ekonomi dengan cara membatasi dan/atau melarang untuk bekerja yang layak di dalam atau  di luar rumah sehingga korban berada di bawah kendali orang tersebut.

translated_text:
Article 9

Neglect as referred to in Article 5 letter d is caused by:
a. acts that result in the unfulfillment of the child's needs properly, whether physical, mental, spiritual or social, carried out by parents, guardians, or any other party responsible for their care;
b. acts of deliberately neglecting to maintain, care for, or take care of the child as appropriate, carried out by parents, guardians, or any other party responsible for their care;
c. acts of neglecting a person within the scope of their household, whereas according to the law applicable to them or because of an agreement or contract they are obliged to provide life, care, or maintenance to that person; and/or
d. acts that result in economic dependence by restricting and/or prohibiting decent work inside or outside the home so that the victim is under the control of that person.

text:
BAB 111

HAK KORBAN

Pasal 12

Setiap Korban mendapatkan hak:
a. untuk dihormati harkat dan martabatnya sebagai manusia;
b. pemulihan kesehatan dan psikologis dari penderitaan yang dialami korban;
c. menentukan sendiri keputusannya;
d. mendsipatkan informasi;
e. kerahasiaan identitasnya;
f. kompensasi;
g. rehabilitasi sosial;
h. penanganan pengaduan;
i. mendapatkan kemudahan dalam proses peradilan; dan/atau
j. pendampingan.

translated_text:
CHAPTER 111

RIGHTS OF VICTIMS

Article 12

Every Victim obtains the right:
a. to have their dignity and honor as a human being respected;
b. health and psychological recovery from the suffering experienced by the victim;
c. to determine their own decisions;
d. to obtain information;
e. confidentiality of their identity;
f. compensation;
g. social rehabilitation;
h. complaint handling;
i. to obtain facilitation in the judicial process; and/or
j. assistance.

text:
Pasal 13

Anak korban kekerasan selain mendapatkan hak sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 12, juga mendapatkan hak khusus, yang terdiri atas:
a. penghormatan atas kelangsungan hidup, tumbuh dan berkembang;
b. pelayanan dasar;
e. perlindungan yang sama;
d. bebas dari berbagai stigma; dan/atau
e. mendapatkan kebebasan.

translated_text:
Article 13

Child victims of violence in addition to obtaining the rights as referred to in Article 12, also obtain special rights, consisting of:
a. respect for survival, growth and development;
b. basic services;
e. equal protection;
d. freedom from various stigma; and/or
e. obtaining freedom.

text:
Pasal 14

1. Pemerintah Daerah wajib dan bertanggung jawab untuk melaksanakan upaya perlindungan perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan melalui:
a. penetapan kebijakan;
b. penyusunan perencanaan program dan kegiatan;
e. pembentukan P2TP2A;
d. memberikan dukungan sarana dan prasarana;
e. mengalokasikan anggaran; dan
f. pembentukan FPKK.
2. Untuk: mengantisipasi terjadinya tindak kekerasan, Pemerintah Daerah menyelenggarakan layanan bagi korban dalam bentuk:
a. memfasilitasi pembentukan P2TP2A;
b. memfasilitasi sarana dan prasarana P2TP2A sesuai kemampuan; dan
c. memfasilitasi FPKK sebagai wadah jejaring penanganan korban.

translated_text:
Article 14

1. The Regional Government is obligated and responsible to implement protection efforts for women and children victims of violence through:
a. policy determination;
b. preparation of program and activity planning;
e. establishment of P2TP2A;
d. providing support for facilities and infrastructure;
e. allocating budget; and
f. establishment of FPKK.
2. To anticipate the occurrence of acts of violence, the Regional Government organizes services for victims in the form of:
a. facilitating the establishment of P2TP2A;
b. facilitating P2TP2A facilities and infrastructure according to capacity; and
c. facilitating FPKK as a network forum for victim handling.

text:
Pasal 16

Masyarakat dan keluarga mempunyai kewajiban dan tanggung jawab yang meliputi:
a. mencegah terjadinya kekerasan terhadap perempuan dan anak;
b. melaporkan bila terjadi kekerasan;
e. melindungi korban; dan
d. memberikan pertolongan darurat.

translated_text:
Article 16

The community and family have obligations and responsibilities which include:
a. preventing the occurrence of violence against women and children;
b. reporting if violence occurs;
e. protecting victims; and
d. providing emergency assistance.

text:
Pasal 19

1. Struktur organisasi P2TP2A yang dibentuk oleh Pemerintah Daerah sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 17 ayat (1) terdiri atas:
a. ketua umum atau sebutan lain yang setingkat;
b. wakil ketua umum;
c. ketua pelaksana;
d. wakil ketua pelaksana;
e. sekretaris;
f. bendahara; dan
g. ketua pelaksana yang membawahi bidang.
3. Ketentuan lebih lanjut mengenai struktur, dan tugas P2TP2A yang dibentuk oleh Daerah sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1)  ditetapkan dengan keputusan Walikota.

translated_text:
Article 19

1. The organizational structure of P2TP2A established by the Regional Government as referred to in Article 17 paragraph (1) consists of:
a. general chairperson or other equivalent designation;
b. deputy general chairperson;
c. executive chairperson;
d. deputy executive chairperson;
e. secretary;
f. treasurer; and
g. executive chairperson overseeing fields.
3. Further provisions regarding the structure and duties of P2TP2A established by the Region as referred to in paragraph (1) are stipulated by Mayor's decree.

text:
Pasal 20

1. P2TP2A yang dibentuk oleh Pemerintah Daerah paling kurang memiliki tiga konselor.
2. Konselor sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) meliputi:
a. konselor dalam bidang hukum;
b. konselor dalam bidang kesehatan; dan
c. konselor dalam bidang psikologi.
3. Pelaksanaan konseling yang dilaksanakan oleh konselor dapat dilaksanakan secara berjejaring sebagai berikut:
a. konseling dalam bidang hukum dengein melibatkan kepolisian, kejaksaan, pengadilan negeri, pengadilan agama, lembaga  advokasi hukum dan Lembaga Swadaya Masyarakat;
b. konseling dalam bidang kesehatan dengan melibatkan Dinas  Kesehatan, Rumah Sakit Umu m Daerah dan layanan kesehatan lainnya;
c. konseling dalam bidang psikologi degan melibatkan pendamping psikologi dan/atau psikolog.

translated_text:
Article 20

1. P2TP2A established by the Regional Government must have at least three counselors.
2. Counselors as referred to in paragraph (1) include:
a. counselor in the field of law;
b. counselor in the field of health; and
c. counselor in the field of psychology.
3. The implementation of counseling carried out by counselors can be implemented in a networked manner as follows:
a. counseling in the field of law by involving the police, prosecutor's office, district court, religious court, legal advocacy institutions and Non-Governmental Organizations;
b. counseling in the field of health by involving the Health Office, Regional General Hospital and other health services;
c. counseling in the field of psychology by involving psychological companions and/or psychologists.

text:
Pasal 21

1. Upaya pencegahan kekerasan terhadap perempuan dan anak dilakukan secara terpadu oleh Pemerintah Daerah yang dikoordinasikan oleh perangkat daerah yang menyelenggarakan urusan pemerintahan di bidang pemberdayaan perempuan dan perlindungan anak.
2. Upaya pencegahan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dilaksanakan dengan cara membentuk jaringan kerja dalam upaya pencegahan kekerasan;
b. melakukan koordinasi, integrasi, sinkronisasi pencegahan kekerasan berdasarkan pola kemitraan;
c. membentuk sistem pencegahan kekerasan;
d. melakukan sosialisasi tentang peraturan perundang-undangan yang berkaitan dengan perlindungan perempuan dan tindak korban  kekerasan; dan
e. memberikan pendidikan kritis tentang hak-hak perempuan dan anak bagi masyarakat.

translated_text:
Article 21

1. Violence prevention efforts against women and children are carried out in an integrated manner by the Regional Government coordinated by the regional apparatus that administers governmental affairs in the field of women's empowerment and child protection.
2. Prevention efforts as referred to in paragraph (1) are implemented by forming a work network in violence prevention efforts;
b. conducting coordination, integration, synchronization of violence prevention based on partnership patterns;
c. forming a violence prevention system;
d. conducting socialization about laws and regulations related to the protection of women and victims of violence; and
e. providing critical education about the rights of women and children for the community.

text:
Pasal 22

Selain Pemerintah Daerah, upaya pencegahan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 21 ayat (1) dilakukan oleh:
a. keluarga dan/atau kerabat terdekat;
b. masyarakat;
c. lembaga pendidikan; dan
d. Lembaga Swadaya Masyarakat.

translated_text:
Article 22

In addition to the Regional Government, prevention efforts as referred to in Article 21 paragraph (1) are carried out by:
a. family and/or closest relatives;
b. community;
c. educational institutions; and
d. Non-Governmental Organizations.

text:
Pasal 24

Penyelenggaraan pelayanan terhadap korban dilaksanakan dengan:
a. cepat;
b. aman dan nyaman;
c. rasa empati;
d. non diskriminasi;
e. mudah dijangkau;
f. tidak dikenakan biaya; dan
g. dijamin kerahasiaannya.

translated_text:
Article 24

The implementation of services to victims is carried out with:
a. speed;
b. safety and comfort;
c. a sense of empathy;
d. non-discrimination;
e. easy accessibility;
f. no charges; and
g. guaranteed confidentiality.

text:
Pasal 25

Bentuk pelayanan terhadap korban meliputi:
a. pelayanan pengaduan, konsultasi, dan konseling;
b. pelayanan pendampingan;
c. pelayanan kesehatan;
d. pelayanan rehabilitasi sosial;
e. pelayanan hukum ; dan
f. pelayanan pemulangan dan reintegrasi sosial.

translated_text:
Article 25

Forms of services to victims include:
a. complaint, consultation, and counseling services;
b. assistance services;
c. health services;
d. social rehabilitation services;
e. legal services; and
f. repatriation and social reintegration services.

text:
Pasal 27

Pelayanan pendampingan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 25 huruf b  meliputi:
a. mendampingi korban selama proses pemeriksaan dan pemulihan kesehatan;
b. mendampingi korban selama proses medicolegal;
c. mendampingi korban selama proses pemeriksaan di Kepolisian, Kejaksaan dan pengadilan;
d. memantau kepentingan dan hak-hak korban dalam proses pemeriksaan di Kepolisan, Kejaksaan dan Pengadilan;
e. menjaga privasi dan kerahasiaan korban dari semua pihak yang tidak berkepentingan, termasuk pemberitaan oleh media massa;
f. melakukan koordinasi dengan pendamping yang lain; dan
g. memberikan penanganan yang berkelanjutan hingga tahap rehabilitasi.

translated_text:
Article 27

Assistance services as referred to in Article 25 letter b include:
a. accompanying victims during the examination and health recovery process;
b. accompanying victims during the medicolegal process;
c. accompanying victims during the examination process at the Police, Prosecutor's Office and court;
d. monitoring the interests and rights of victims in the examination process at the Police, Prosecutor's Office and Court;
e. maintaining the privacy and confidentiality of victims from all parties who have no interest, including coverage by mass media;
f. conducting coordination with other companions; and
g. providing continuous handling up to the rehabilitation stage.

text:
Pasal 30

1. Pelayanan hukum sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 25 huruf e dalam  rangka membantu korban dalam menjalani proses peradilan.
2. Pelayanan hukum sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dalam bentuk:
a. memberikan konsultas i hukum yang mencakup informasi mengenai hak-hak korban dan proses peradilan;
b. mendampingi korban di tingkat penyidikan, penuntutan, dan  pemeriksaan dalam sidang pengadilan dan membantu korban untuk secara lengkap memaparkan kekerasan yang dialaminya;
c. melakukan koordinasi dengan sesama penegak hukum, relawan  pendamping, dan pekerja sosial agar proses peradilan berjalan sebaigaimana mestinya.

translated_text:
Article 30

1. Legal services as referred to in Article 25 letter e are intended to assist victims in undergoing the judicial process.
2. Legal services as referred to in paragraph (1) are in the form of:
a. providing legal consultation that includes information regarding victims' rights and the judicial process;
b. accompanying victims at the investigation, prosecution, and court hearing examination levels and assisting victims to fully describe the violence they have experienced;
c. coordinating with fellow law enforcers, volunteer companions, and social workers so that the judicial process proceeds as it should.

text:
Pasal 38

Tugas dem fungsi FPKK sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 37 ayat (1) yaitu:
a. mengoordinasikan dan menyinkronkan pencegahan, pelayanan, dan pemberdayaan terhadap korban kekerasan perempuan dan anak;
b. memelihara dan mengembangkan FPKK: dalam pencegahan, pelayanan, dan pemberdayaan korban kekerasan secara berjejaring serta sistem rujukan;
c. melakukan pendidikan tentang nilai-nilai non diskriminasi terhadap perempuan dan anak;
d. melakukan sosialisasi peraturan perundang- undangan yang berkaitan dengan penyelenggaraan perlindungan perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan;
e. mengumpulkan, menyusun, dan menyajikan laporan data korban kekerasan; dan
f. melakukan pemantauan dan evaluasi terhadap penyelenggaraan perlindungan perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan.

translated_text:
Article 38

The duties and functions of FPKK as referred to in Article 37 paragraph (1) are:
a. coordinating and synchronizing prevention, services, and empowerment of women and child victims of violence;
b. maintaining and developing FPKK in the prevention, services, and empowerment of victims of violence in a networked manner and referral system;
c. conducting education on non-discrimination values toward women and children;
d. conducting socialization of laws and regulations related to the implementation of protection of women and child victims of violence;
e. collecting, compiling, and presenting data reports on victims of violence; and
f. conducting monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of protection of women and child victims of violence.
